But measuring 
\begin_inset Formula $B_{p}$
\end_inset

 along with 
\begin_inset Formula $A_{v}$
\end_inset

 doesn't resolve all ambiguities; consider a loop of flipped spins that
 extends all the way around the edge of the lattice (i.e., wraps around an
 axis of the torus).
 Applying 
\begin_inset Formula $B_{p}$
\end_inset

 to each particle along such a loop would simply shift the loop laterally.
 
\series bold
Thus, we have found the set of undetectable errors for this coding scheme
\series default
, i.e., the set 
\begin_inset Formula $\left\{ \bar{X_{1}},\bar{X_{2}},\bar{Z_{1}},\bar{Z_{2}}\right\} $
\end_inset

